tch, she switched gears and won easily in a world record 1:54.94. The first four runners also surpassed Gerasimova’s world record in the fastest women’s 800 race ever run to that date. Four days later Kazankina returned to add the 1,500 and win the 800/1,500 double."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "340"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77216"} "Tatyana Kazankina"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "2:00.15 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "1:57.49 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:54.94 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "45"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/65697"} "Nikolina Shtereva"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BUL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BUL.png"}] "BUL"]] [:td {} "2:01.02 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "1:57.35 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "1:55.42 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "168"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69725"} "Elfi Zinn"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "2:01.54 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "1:57.56 (3 h2)"] [:td {} "1:55.60 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "166"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69633"} "Anita Weiß"]] 